# SYNOPSIS
# --------
# Test the <stats_command>_reset and <status_command>_reset requests of ldmsd.
#
# Each stats|status request that has the optional reset attribute has a reset-only
# counterpart. The stats|status requests themselves do not reset the
# statistics. The test collects activity on an aggregator, resets the
# statistics with the new request, and verifies that:
#
#   - the reset request succeeds and replies "OK" (it returns no statistics);
#   - the statistics reported by the corresponding stats|status request are
#     reset;
#   - the stats|status requests do not reset the statistics, even if the
#     deprecated `reset` attribute is given;
#   - ldmsd logs a message that suggests the reset request to use if the
#     deprecated `reset` or `hist_recalibrate` attribute is given.
#
# Tested requests:
#
#   xprt_stats_reset, thread_stats_reset, profiling_reset,
#   update_time_stats_reset, store_time_stats_reset,
#   stream_status_reset, stream_client_dump_reset,
#   msg_stats_reset, msg_client_stats_reset
#
# Cluster:
#
#   samplerd (meminfo) <--- agg (updater + store_csv)
#
# All the requests are sent to `agg`.

